menu-placement-primary = Top-level context menu
menu-placement-nested = MetaFlow submenu

metadata-update-saved-description = Update Metadata uses this saved policy. Check and Repair fills empty ordinary fields without changing item types. The separate author-repair switch below controls author correction in both manual actions.
metadata-repair-creators =
    .label = Repair authors from verified metadata, including missing, partial and incorrect lists
metadata-repair-creators-description = Both manual actions fetch and correct authors even in blank-field mode; the combined workflow requires the author-check rule. Only identity-matched, valid creators are written, and edits made while waiting are preserved. Disable to use the original blank/overwrite policy. Automatic imports remain blank-only.

menu-placement-none = None (hidden)
batch-feedback-heading = Run feedback and reports
batch-feedback-auto-report =
    .label = Automatically open detailed reports after a run
batch-feedback-description = Detailed reports stay closed by default. Results, warnings and field changes are kept for this session and can be opened on demand. Progress notifications use the separate setting above.
batch-feedback-view-report =
    .label = View last run report
batch-feedback-empty = No run results in this session.
batch-feedback-summary = Last run: { $total } items, { $saved } saved, { $failed } failed, { $warnings } warnings.

index-source-heading = ESI and Nature Index: source priority
index-source-esi = ESI discipline source
index-source-nature = Nature Index source
index-source-api-first = API first, then local database
index-source-local-first = Local database first, then API
index-source-api-only = API only
index-source-local-only = Local database only
index-source-description = Configure each independently. API uses the existing EasyScholar key; local uses your custom or bundled database. Selecting an item reads cached/local results without network requests. Run an index query or EasyScholar update to fetch API data. The default is local only.
index-source-nature-uuid = Nature Index custom dataset UUID (optional)
index-source-nature-description = Enable the Nature Index dataset in your EasyScholar account. A UUID selects it exactly; otherwise its returned dataset name is matched. Missing data does not mean nonmembership. The pane shows the dataset name; check whether it is the 82-journal or 145-journal edition.

